cartridge "SNAKE BITE/KEN HUEBNER/1990"
' SNAKE BITE ("JUMP'N SNAKES, CATCH'N MICE") - Ken Huebner, Commodore 128
' (BASIC 7 + 1,620 bytes of machine code), ReRUN March/April 1990.
' ColecoVision port in Amy. The rules are the C128 machine code's, step for
' step, in the C128's own coordinates (multicolour x 0-159, bitmap y 0-199):
' see README.md and orig/ml.dis. One pass of MlStep = one C128 IRQ (jiffy).
'
' The game: a kid on a pogo stick hops around a classroom (the hop never
' stops: 24 frames, 2 of them on the floor). Catch the loose mice: land next
' to one. Snakes slither everywhere; land on one and it bites. The stick
' steers: the direction held during a hop is taken on landing and kept for the
' whole next hop. The teacher comes back when the time runs out. 10
' classrooms, 3 lives.
'
' Layout: HUD row 1, heart border rows 2 and 22 / columns 2 and 29, the
' field columns 3-28 x rows 3-21 is a bitmap of unique tiles (RN[] in
' gen.py): snakes are drawn into it pixel by pixel, and the C128's collision
' test (shadow sprite against the snake pixels) reads it back.

